{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 30, :comments ["<b>For his compassion grew warm.</b> He asked him: Do you have a brother from the same mother? He said to him: I had a brother, and I do not know where he is. Do you have sons? He said to him: I have ten. He said to him: What are their names? He said to him: Bela and Becher, etc. He said: What is the meaning of these names? He said to him: All of them are named for my brother and the troubles that befell him — Bela, because he was swallowed up (נִבְלַע) among the nations; Becher, because he was the firstborn (בְּכוֹר) of my mother; Ashbel, because El took him captive (שְׁבָאוֹ אֵל); Gera, because he sojourned (גָּר) in a lodging; Naaman, because he was exceedingly pleasant (נָעִים); Ehi and Rosh — he was my brother (אָחִי), and he was my chief (רֹאשִׁי); Muppim — from my father's mouth (מִפִּי אָבִי) I learned; Huppim — because he did not see my wedding (חֻפָּתִי) and I did not see his wedding (חֻפָּתוֹ); Ard — because he went down (יָרַד) among the nations — as is found in tractate Sotah. Immediately his compassion grew warm." "<b>Grew warm.</b> Grew warm. And in the language of the Mishnah: עַל הַכֹּמֶר שֶׁל זֵיתִים; and in Aramaic: בְּמִכְמַר בִּשְׂרָא. And in Scripture: ״עוֹרֵנוּ כְּתַנּוּר נִכְמָרוּ״ (Lamentations 5) — they grew warm and shriveled, shriveled from the heat of famine. So too with any skin: when it is heated it shrivels and contracts."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 43, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:03:27.772506731Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}